        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://auburnboroughpa.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first house in Auburn was built in the late 1830s by boatman Samuel Moyer, who also ran the town’s first store.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburn%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Schuylkill River cuts through Auburn, providing a natural waterway that shaped early settlement patterns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburn%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Auburn’s terrain is steeply hilly to the north and gently rolling to the south, giving the borough a varied landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
